<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_LeaningScrub_Biome.xml                  LEANINGSCRUB_RM_MOD_BUILD_1

    Phase A row 9 of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md — the
    RimMandrake-tier twin of the frozen src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/
    BiomeDefs/RUT_AridShrubland.xml, generalized to zero campaign-specific
    content per §3a's test. Full sheet (campaign-side):
    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/arid_shrubland.md (FROZEN).

    Copied from the frozen def, MEASURED 2026-09-25: terrain thresholds,
    weather commonalities, disease table and animalDensity/plantDensity/
    forageability/movementDifficulty/diseaseMtbDays/wildPlantRegrowDays are
    all byte-identical to RUT_AridShrubland.xml's own values — nothing here
    is re-derived. workerClass stays RimWorld.BiomeWorker_AridShrubland
    (vanilla Core, confirmed via the installed game's own
    Biomes_WarmArid.xml) — a donor type in workerClass would be a hard
    dependency the RimMandrake tier may not assume, but this one is Core
    itself, so no RM_BiomeWorker_LeaningScrub wrapper is owed.

    <texture> is vanilla Core's own "World/Biomes/AridShrubland" (MEASURED
    from Biomes_WarmArid.xml on the installed game), NOT the frozen twin's
    "World/Biomes/AridShrubland1" — that suffixed variant belongs to a
    Workshop donor mod (id 3546956014), and this mod ships standalone.

    wildAnimals: every RSW_/SW_/donor-Star-Wars-name entry stays OUT (per
    §7 Q11, "RimMandrake should not name star wars ever") and rides
    src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_LeaningScrub.xml
    instead. Only 4 non-Star-Wars donor rows from the frozen def
    are inline here (Q9: non-Star-Wars donor fauna is acceptable inline).

    wildPlants: the frozen def's own RUT_-prefixed plant defs (RUT_Fuzz,
    RUT_Grellbush, RUT_Grellspine, RUT_WildHealroot, RUT_SweetlineTree,
    formerly mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora) are renamed to this mod's RM_ tier
    per §7 Q8 ("mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora: DISSOLVE IT. Each plant moves
    into the RimMandrake mod of the biome whose wildPlants lists it,
    renamed RM_"). 🔑 The ORIGINAL RUT_-prefixed defs are left standing,
    UNTOUCHED, inside mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora: the frozen
    RUT_AridShrubland.xml's own wildPlants block still names them under
    MayRequire="mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora", and that mod carries the
    player's live world until Phase B deletes RUT_AridShrubland.xml
    outright (biome_mod_architecture.md §5's hazard section — a defName a
    frozen def depends on cannot be pulled out from under it before then).
    So mandrake.rut.ashkarrflora is not literally dissolved THIS pass; it
    is frozen alongside its biome, exactly the same bounded-duplication
    pattern §5 step 3 already uses for the biome def itself, and its real
    deletion is scheduled for Phase B step 4 together with
    RUT_AridShrubland.xml. This is the one deliberate deviation from the
    item's literal "move" wording, made to avoid the exact hazard §5
    documents for biome defs, applied one level down to a def a frozen
    biome depends on.

    RSW_JekkaGrass / Plant_Nysyllin_Wild / RSW_TanniVine /
    RSW_RuzzoCarpet / RSW_QuissaBloom carry no MayRequire in the
    frozen def either — copied byte-identical; fixing that donor-gating gap
    is not this item's scope.

    Art: RM_Fuzz/RM_Grellbush/RM_Grellspine/RM_WildHealroot carry the four
    finished RUT_ renders (rutfuzz_v1, rut_grellbush, rut_grellspine,
    rut_wildhealroot), copied under Textures/Things/Plant/RM_<Name>/ by
    LEANINGSCRUB_RULED_CONTENT_1. RM_SweetlineTree's 14-variant art is copied
    and renamed alongside its def (see Textures/Things/Plant/RM_SweetlineTree/).

    LEANINGSCRUB_RULED_CONTENT_1 added the ruled cast to the rosters below:
    13 animals (RM_LeaningScrubFauna.xml), 4 fuzz flora
    (RM_LeaningScrubFuzzFlora.xml) and 4 venomvine forms
    (RM_LeaningScrubVenomvineForms.xml). Their art is queued in artpipe
    (leaningscrub_bedazzle_cast.csv), not yet wired - placeholders until then.
    Commonalities are design proposals. RM_Blurrg is deliberately absent: it
    is tamed-only, never wild. The donor rows above stay until the roster
    audit rules on them.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_LeaningScrub</defName>
    <label>the Leaning Scrub</label>
    <description>Knee-high silver-green fuzz at eerily even spacing, running unbroken to every horizon, all of it leaning the same way, all of it moving - because the wind never stops. Sightlines are gone under the fuzz-canopy and cover is everywhere, for everything smaller than a person, all the time.</description>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.BiomeWorker_AridShrubland</workerClass>
    <texture>World/Biomes/RM_LeaningScrub</texture>
    <riverbankTerrain>Riverbank</riverbankTerrain>
    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>false</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.8</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.35</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.5</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>1</movementDifficulty>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalFlu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_AnimalPlague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_OrganDecay</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>10</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>Sand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.45</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>Soil</terrain>
        <min>0.45</min>
        <max>0.9</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>SoilRich</terrain>
        <min>0.9</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 part 1: ban 5 (every ordinary day carries
         wind) - the stock Clear 30 / Fog 45 are replaced by the owned windy twins
         RM_ScrubWind / RM_ScrubWindFog (Defs/WeatherDefs/RM_LeaningScrub_Weather.xml),
         and the Stall and the Gale take their share from them. -->
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <RM_ScrubWind>28</RM_ScrubWind>
      <RM_ScrubWindFog>40</RM_ScrubWindFog>
      <RM_Stall>3</RM_Stall>
      <RM_Gale>7</RM_Gale>
      <!-- SCRUB_WIND_BUILD_LEAN_ON_PURPOSE part 3 (owner card 2026-10-20): the windy twins replace stock DryThunderstorm,
           GrayPall and Overcast at the same commonalities (WeatherDefs/RM_LeaningScrub_WindyTwins.xml). -->
      <RM_ScrubDryThunderstorm>1</RM_ScrubDryThunderstorm>
      <SnowGentle>0</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>0</SnowHard>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <RM_ScrubGrayPall MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">1</RM_ScrubGrayPall>
      <RM_ScrubOvercast>5</RM_ScrubOvercast>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <RM_Vurra MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.7</RM_Vurra>  <!-- vurra - our port of the donor terrorworm (RSW_DesertPortMisc_Races.xml), Q9 -->
      <RM_Chikka MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.25</RM_Chikka>  <!-- cactipine - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <RM_Durrok MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.1</RM_Durrok>  <!-- wildpawn - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <RM_Mullgoth MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.025</RM_Mullgoth>  <!-- wildpod - non-Star-Wars donor, Q9 -->
      <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_RULED_CONTENT_1: the ruled cast (RM_LeaningScrubFauna.xml) -->
      <RM_Fuzzrunner>1.0</RM_Fuzzrunner>
      <RM_Thornhold>0.4</RM_Thornhold>
      <RM_Shokka>0.15</RM_Shokka>
      <RM_Zellik>0.3</RM_Zellik>
      <RM_Fuzzviper>0.3</RM_Fuzzviper>
      <RM_Surrik>0.4</RM_Surrik>
      <RM_Ribbonwhip>0.3</RM_Ribbonwhip>
      <RM_Vissler>0.2</RM_Vissler>
      <RM_Dustflutter>0.5</RM_Dustflutter>
      <RM_Shirrel>0.25</RM_Shirrel>
      <!-- LONGSHADE_SHEET_STRUCTURAL_RULINGS_1 (owner 2026-10-04, Long Shade sheet: "Move this to the biome with all the Fuzz (Leaning?), Rim Mandrake level."): the truffle mole, moved here from the Long Shade; def stays in mandrake.rm.longshade (same composed mod). Weight carried over verbatim from its Long Shade row; PROVISIONAL. -->
      <RM_TruffleMole MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">0.5</RM_TruffleMole>
      <RM_Crustweevil>0.6</RM_Crustweevil>
      <RM_Rollbug>0.4</RM_Rollbug>
      <RM_Tikkit>0.5</RM_Tikkit>
      <RM_TunnelSnake>0.5</RM_TunnelSnake>  <!-- the yanker, ported from RSW_TunnelSnake (owner note on the Leaning Scrub sheet 2026-10-06: RimMandrake tier); same 0.5 the patch layer gave it -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <RM_Fuzz>0.9</RM_Fuzz>  <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_RM_MOD_BUILD_1: renamed from RUT_Fuzz, §7 Q8 -->
      <RSW_JekkaGrass MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.5</RSW_JekkaGrass>  <!-- grass -->
      <!-- Plant_Brambles CUT from this roster: owner 2026-10-19 by card ("Cut them as the card said": the eight vanilla/DLC rows), item REGEN_GAPS_DECIDE_STRAYS_AND_FLYERS. -->
      <RM_Grellbush>0.3</RM_Grellbush>  <!-- renamed from RUT_Grellbush, §7 Q8 -->
      <RM_Grellspine>0.3</RM_Grellspine>  <!-- renamed from RUT_Grellspine, §7 Q8 -->
      <RM_WildHealroot>0.25</RM_WildHealroot>  <!-- renamed from RUT_WildHealroot, §7 Q8; label kept "wild healroot" -->
      <RSW_Plant_Nysyllin_Wild MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.22</RSW_Plant_Nysyllin_Wild>  <!-- wild nysyllin plant; not IP per Q11a -->
      <RSW_TanniVine MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_TanniVine>  <!-- creep stern -->
      <RSW_RuzzoCarpet MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_RuzzoCarpet>  <!-- crimson cushion -->
      <RSW_QuissaBloom MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">0.2</RSW_QuissaBloom>  <!-- dervish -->
      <RM_VenomvineThicket>0.15</RM_VenomvineThicket>  <!-- fortress flora, already RimMandrake-tier, no move -->
      <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_RULED_CONTENT_1: fuzz flora and venomvine forms -->
      <RM_Whipfuzz>0.6</RM_Whipfuzz>
      <RM_Pillowmoss>0.2</RM_Pillowmoss>
      <RM_Tanglefuzz>0.2</RM_Tanglefuzz>
      <RM_Cruststar>0.3</RM_Cruststar>
      <RM_DrippingVenomvine>0.05</RM_DrippingVenomvine>
      <RM_TwitcherVenomvine>0.05</RM_TwitcherVenomvine>
      <RM_HollowVenomvine>0.04</RM_HollowVenomvine>
      <RM_CrownVenomvine>0.002</RM_CrownVenomvine>
      <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_VENOMVINE_FORMS_PITCH_1: the six further forms (owner, 2026-10-03), rare like
           the four above. PROVISIONAL. Sworn is lowest: wild sworn hedges are dead settlements' leavings. -->
      <RM_RearingVenomvine>0.03</RM_RearingVenomvine>
      <RM_WalkingVenomvine>0.02</RM_WalkingVenomvine>
      <RM_HoardVenomvine>0.02</RM_HoardVenomvine>
      <RM_QuenchVenomvine>0.03</RM_QuenchVenomvine>
      <RM_SwornVenomvine>0.005</RM_SwornVenomvine>
      <RM_SheddingVenomvine>0.02</RM_SheddingVenomvine>
      <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_SLEEPER_VINE_1: looks dead until a body of size >= 0.5 passes. PROVISIONAL placement, rare -->
      <RM_SleeperVenomvine>0.01</RM_SleeperVenomvine>
      <!-- VENOMVINE_BUILD_SCRUB_GROWS_TEETH Q4 (owner card 2026-10-16): Strangler, Weeper and Lure go on the wild list.
           Weights low on purpose: the island map step's rooms place most of them, not scatter. PROVISIONAL. -->
      <RM_StranglerVenomvine>0.005</RM_StranglerVenomvine>
      <RM_WeeperVenomvine>0.005</RM_WeeperVenomvine>
      <RM_LureVenomvine>0.005</RM_LureVenomvine>
      <RM_Salvessa>0.22</RM_Salvessa>  <!-- PLANT_TIERS_RECONCILE_MOST_ARE_BAROQUE: franchise-free base of RSW_Plant_Nysyllin_Wild; same weight as that canon row, which still injects on top when SW is loaded -->
    </wildPlants>
    <!-- RM_SweetlineTree is a landmark, not scatter: it is NOT in wildPlants. It reaches maps
         only through the RM_SweetlineTrees map step below (owner ruling R13, 2026-10-03: a rare
         map step plants one or two per Leaning Scrub map) or a dev spawn. -->
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>27</wildPlantRegrowDays>
    <!-- SWEETLINE_TREE_MAP_STEP_1: 1-2 sweetline trees on a share of new maps (Mod Setting). -->
    <extraGenSteps>
      <li>RM_SweetlineTrees</li>
      <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 part 8: ruins and living camps (Source/RM_ScrubInjections.cs). -->
      <li>RM_ScrubInjections</li>
      <!-- VENOMVINE_BUILD_SCRUB_GROWS_TEETH Q1/Q4: venomvine islands with rooms (Source/RM_VenomvineIslands.cs). -->
      <li>RM_VenomvineIslands</li>
    </extraGenSteps>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- LEANINGSCRUB_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 part 2: the Lean - each map locks one wind
           heading (Source/RM_TheLean.cs). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.LeaningScrub.RM_LeanExtension">
        <!-- SCRUB_WIND_BUILD_LEAN_ON_PURPOSE part 1 (owner card 2026-10-20): these fuzz and scrub plants face the map's
             wind instead of mirroring at random (Source/RM_PlantLean.cs). Venomvine forms and trees stay vanilla. -->
        <leanPlants>
          <li>RM_Fuzz</li>
          <li>RM_Whipfuzz</li>
          <li>RM_Tanglefuzz</li>
          <li>RM_Pillowmoss</li>
          <li>RM_Grellbush</li>
          <li>RM_Grellspine</li>
          <li>RM_Cruststar</li>
        </leanPlants>
        <!-- Variants whose own art leans west (top drawn left of the base). MEASURED from the PNGs 2026-10-20; every
             listed plant's other variants lean east or stand upright. selftest_scrub_wind.py re-measures this list. -->
        <westLeaningTextures>
          <li>RM_Fuzz_c</li>
          <li>RM_Fuzz_e</li>
          <li>RM_Whipfuzz_c</li>
          <li>RM_Pillowmoss_c</li>
          <li>RM_Grellbush_a</li>
          <li>RM_Grellspine_b</li>
          <li>RM_Grellspine_c</li>
          <li>RM_Cruststar_d</li>
        </westLeaningTextures>
        <!-- Owner card 2026-10-20 17:28 ("Wind dir -> Point it at the sun, snap to a side"): the wind blows from the tile
             toward the substellar point; Ash'karr's is (0, 0), as in RM_PinnedSunExtension and the WeatherSuite. -->
        <substellarLatitude>0</substellarLatitude>
        <substellarLongitude>0</substellarLongitude>
      </li>
      <!-- VENOMVINE_BUILD_SCRUB_GROWS_TEETH (design/RimMandrake/venomvine_design_2026-10-16.md §10 RULED): this biome grows
           venomvine islands (about 15% of open ground, Q1) with rarer forms as rooms (Q4), and lets venomvine creep slowly
           downwind to a map cap (22%, Q3). Room roles: §5 "room?" column. Numbers here are shape, PROVISIONAL; the
           player's numbers are Mod Settings. Sworn is absent on purpose (hedge homesteads only, never a wild island). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.LeaningScrub.RM_VenomvineIslandsExtension">
        <thicketDef>RM_VenomvineThicket</thicketDef>
        <crownDef>RM_CrownVenomvine</crownDef>
        <countedForms>
          <li>RM_SwornVenomvine</li>
          <li>RM_SleeperVenomvineAwake</li>
        </countedForms>
        <rooms>
          <li><form>RM_DrippingVenomvine</form><role>edge</role><weight>1.0</weight><cells>3~6</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_TwitcherVenomvine</form><role>edge</role><weight>1.0</weight><cells>1~3</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_HollowVenomvine</form><role>interior</role><weight>0.8</weight><cells>4~10</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_RearingVenomvine</form><role>edge</role><weight>0.6</weight><cells>3~6</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_WalkingVenomvine</form><role>downwind</role><weight>0.4</weight><cells>3~6</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_HoardVenomvine</form><role>interior</role><weight>0.4</weight><cells>1~3</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_QuenchVenomvine</form><role>interior</role><weight>0.6</weight><cells>2~4</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_SheddingVenomvine</form><role>downwind</role><weight>0.4</weight><cells>3~6</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_StranglerVenomvine</form><role>edge</role><weight>0.4</weight><cells>2~4</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_WeeperVenomvine</form><role>interior</role><weight>0.4</weight><cells>2~4</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_SleeperVenomvine</form><role>interior</role><weight>0.3</weight><cells>2~5</cells></li>
          <li><form>RM_LureVenomvine</form><role>edge</role><weight>0.5</weight><cells>2~4</cells></li>
        </rooms>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
